## CalibrationOS vendoring

The markdown in this directory is an unmodified copy of the Impeccable skill
(version 4.8.0, as recorded in `SKILL.md`) from
https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable at commit
`d34c87e1a00989ae8dbdd7f6b30b70f23319e860`.

**Copyright 2025 Paul Bakaus.** Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The license text is `LICENSE` in this directory. Upstream paths named
`skill/reference/` in the notice above correspond to `reference/` here.

Not included, on purpose: the skill's `scripts/` directory (engine launcher,
live-browser bundle, font index). Those are the Impeccable CLI runtime, not
design guidance, and CalibrationOS does not take a runtime dependency on the
`impeccable` npm package. When `SKILL.md` asks to run `scripts/impeccable`,
follow its "Launcher unavailable" path instead of downloading a binary or
adding a package. A one-off scan is `npx impeccable detect` and is not a
project dependency.

CalibrationOS-specific brand notes live in `.cursor/rules/impeccable-design.mdc`
and in the design section of `CLAUDE.md`. They are not part of the upstream work.
